  "answer": "The query asks why disturbed systems oscillate and how coupled vibrations produce waves. R16 (8.03SC: Physics III: Vibrations and Waves) directly addresses both points: it states that when a system is disturbed from stable equilibrium the resulting motion is waves and vibrations, and that waves arise from many interconnected, coupled objects vibrating together. R02 (8.01SC: Classical Mechanics) covers oscillations and normal modes as part of core mechanics, providing the foundational force and energy framework. R18 (2.001: Mechanics & Materials I) introduces solid mechanics and vibration of structures, which can supplement the coupled-systems perspective.",
